<title>USA: Texas Instruments completes sale to Raytheon.</title>
<headline>Texas Instruments completes sale to Raytheon.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texas Instruments Inc said Friday that it has completed the sale of its defense business to Raytheon Co for $2.95 billion, cash.</p>
<p>The company said it plans to use the proceeds to strengthen its focus on digital signal processing solutions. These semiconductor products are used in a wide variety of electronic end-equipment, including high-speed modems, cellular phones, pagers, computers, disk drives, and fax machines.</p>
</text>
